# Prompt Engineering Standards

Guidelines for creating, editing, and validating prompts in the AgentSaasy_NGAI Prompt Library.
This project uses **Anthropic's XML-tagged prompt structure** as its single standard for all prompt content sections. XML tags create unambiguous section boundaries that prevent the model from confusing identity with instructions, tools with guidelines, or examples with directives.

---

## 1. Prompt Categories

Every prompt belongs to exactly one category defined in `prompts/registry.yaml`:

| Category | Purpose | Content Header | Required XML Tags | Example |
|----------|---------|----------------|-------------------|---------|
| `system` | Agent identity & behavior | `## Prompt` | `<identity>`, `<tools>`, `<guidelines>`, `<reasoning_pattern>`, `<output_format>` | `system_asset_agent.md` |
| `demo` | Demo orchestration | `## Prompt` | `<narrative>`, `<acts>`, `<transitions>`, `<pacing>` | `demo_master_showcase.md` |
| `act` | Individual demo scene | `## System Prompt` | `<role>`, `<scenario>`, `<tools_to_use>`, `<talking_point>`, `<transition>` | `act1_iot_anomaly.md` |
| `query` | Reusable user queries | `## Prompt` | `<instructions>`, `<output_format>` | `query_critical_assets.md` |
| `generation` | Long-form document briefs | `## Generation Brief` | `<role>`, `<tone>`, `<document_structure>`, `<formatting>`, `<sources>` | `white_paper_prompt.md` |

When adding a new category, define it in the `categories:` block of `registry.yaml` first.

---

## 2. Canonical Template Structure

Every prompt file MUST include these sections in this order:

### 2.1 — Title Line (H1)

```markdown
# [Category Label]: [Descriptive Name]
```

Format by category:
- **system**: `# System Prompt: [Name]`
- **demo**: `# Demo Master Prompt: [Name]`
- **act**: `# Act [N] — [Name] ([Time])`
- **query**: `# Query Template: [Name]`
- **generation**: `# Generation Brief: [Name]`

### 2.2 — Metadata Line (blockquote, immediately after title)

```markdown
> **ID:** `slug-id` | **Version:** X.Y.Z | **Category:** category_name
```

Rules:
- `ID` must match the `id` field in `registry.yaml` exactly
- `Version` follows semantic versioning (MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH)
- `Category` must be one of the defined categories

### 2.3 — Purpose Section (optional but recommended for complex prompts)

```markdown
## Purpose

One to three sentences explaining what this prompt does,
when to use it, and what kind of output it produces.
```

Required for: `system`, `demo`, `generation` categories.
Optional for: `act`, `query` (these are self-explanatory from title).

### 2.4 — Variables Section

```markdown
## Variables

| Variable | Description | Default |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| `{{variable_name}}` | What it controls | default_value |
```

Rules:
- Use `{{double_braces}}` syntax — matches `PromptLibrary.render()`
- Variable names are `snake_case`
- If no variables: write `None — this is a static [system/query] prompt.`
- Every variable listed here MUST appear in the prompt body
- Every `{{variable}}` in the prompt body MUST be listed here
- The same variables MUST be listed in `registry.yaml` under the prompt entry

### 2.5 — Main Content Section

The header varies by category (see table in Section 1). This is where the actual prompt text lives. Structure the content clearly with subsections.

### 2.6 — Usage Section (required for all prompts)

```markdown
## Usage

```python
from prompt_library import PromptLibrary
lib = PromptLibrary()
prompt = lib.render("slug-id", variable_name="value")
```
```

Shows exactly how to load and render the prompt programmatically.

