## 3. Registry Alignment

Every prompt file MUST have a corresponding entry in `prompts/registry.yaml`.

### Required Fields

```yaml
- id: "slug-id"                    # Unique, matches filename pattern
  name: "Human-Readable Name"      # Descriptive title
  file: "filename.md"              # Actual file in prompts/
  version: "1.0.0"                 # Semantic version
  category: "system"               # One of: system, demo, act, query, generation
  description: >                   # Multi-line description
    What this prompt does and when to use it.
  model: "gpt-4o-mini"            # Recommended model
  est_tokens: 450                  # Estimated token count
  variables:                       # List of {{variables}} or empty []
    - "{{variable_name}}"
  author: "AgentSaasy Team"        # Author
  created: "YYYY-MM-DD"            # Creation date
```

### Consistency Checks

When creating or editing a prompt, verify:
- [ ] `id` in YAML matches `ID` in the .md metadata line
- [ ] `file` in YAML matches the actual filename
- [ ] `version` in YAML matches `Version` in the .md metadata line
- [ ] `category` in YAML matches `Category` in the .md metadata line
- [ ] `variables` list in YAML matches the `## Variables` table in the .md
- [ ] `model` is appropriate for the prompt complexity

### Model Selection Guide

| Category | Default Model | When to Upgrade |
|----------|--------------|-----------------|
| `system` | gpt-4o-mini | Never — runs per conversation |
| `demo` | gpt-4o-mini | Never — real-time demo speed |
| `act` | gpt-4o-mini | Never — real-time demo speed |
| `query` | gpt-4o-mini | Complex multi-tool chains |
| `generation` | gpt-4o | Long-form docs need high-context model |

