## 5. Validation Checklist

Run this checklist before committing any new or modified prompt.

### Structure Validation

- [ ] **H1 title** follows category naming convention
- [ ] **Metadata line** present with ID, Version, Category
- [ ] **Variables section** present (even if "None")
- [ ] **Main content section** uses correct header for category
- [ ] **Usage section** present with working code example
- [ ] **No orphan variables** — every `{{var}}` in body is in the Variables table
- [ ] **No phantom variables** — every variable in the table appears in the body

### Registry Validation

- [ ] **Entry exists** in `prompts/registry.yaml`
- [ ] **ID matches** between .md metadata and YAML entry
- [ ] **Version matches** between .md metadata and YAML entry
- [ ] **Category matches** between .md metadata and YAML entry
- [ ] **Variables match** between .md table and YAML list
- [ ] **File field** points to correct filename
- [ ] **est_tokens** is a reasonable estimate

### XML Tag Validation

- [ ] **Tags present** — prompt body uses XML tags per category requirements (Section 4.2)
- [ ] **Tags matched** — every opening `<tag>` has a closing `</tag>`
- [ ] **Tags named descriptively** — tag names reflect their content (`<tools>`, not `<section2>`)
- [ ] **No markdown headers inside XML sections** — use plain text or nested tags within XML blocks
- [ ] **Variable data wrapped** — any `{{variable}}` with substantial content is inside descriptive tags

### Content Quality

- [ ] **Role is clear** — identity established in `<identity>` or `<role>` tags
- [ ] **Instructions are imperative** — "Analyze", "Generate", not "You could try to..."
- [ ] **Output format specified** — `<output_format>` tag tells model exactly what structure to produce
- [ ] **Domain language correct** — uses PROJECT-DICTIONARY.md terminology
- [ ] **Claims are grounded** — metrics reference specific tools or calculations
- [ ] **No ambiguity** — numbers, formats, and constraints are explicit
- [ ] **Fabrication guardrail** — system prompts include "never fabricate metrics" directive

### Category-Specific Checks

**system prompts:**
- [ ] Has `<identity>`, `<tools>`, `<guidelines>`, `<reasoning_pattern>`, `<output_format>` tags
- [ ] Each tool in `<tools>` has a "Use when:" trigger line
- [ ] Has at least one `<example>` block with `<user_query>` and `<ideal_approach>`

**act prompts:**
- [ ] Has `<role>`, `<scenario>`, `<tools_to_use>` tags
- [ ] Has `<talking_point>` (quotable line for demos)
- [ ] Has `<transition>` (bridge to next act)

**query prompts:**
- [ ] Has `<instructions>` and `<output_format>` tags
- [ ] Self-contained — works without additional context
- [ ] Specifies prioritization or ordering criteria

**demo prompts:**
- [ ] Has `<narrative>`, `<acts>`, `<transitions>`, `<pacing>` tags
- [ ] Has opening and closing statements

**generation prompts:**
- [ ] Has `<role>`, `<tone>`, `<document_structure>`, `<formatting>`, `<sources>` tags
- [ ] Defines tone and voice explicitly in `<tone>`
- [ ] Specifies document structure with section-by-section guidance in `<document_structure>`

